Actually MR doesn't seem to protect against magic traps.  Maybe there are some
effects it protects from, but it's still happy to blind you and bringing a
load of monsters.

MR also doesn't protect from wands of sleep, so a gnome with the wand can be
an "instadeath" for a low level character, which SDSM would have protected
from.

I used to think the choice for GDSM was clear since it'd suck to lose wished
for SDSM to a polytrap; I've since learned that the dragon armor comes back.

I'd still wish for the GDSM, though.  Sokoban aside, amulets or shields of
reflection are often lying around somewhere.  And amulets polymorph into
amulets.  I almost never see CoMR around (though I saw a couple on Astral in
my last ascension, big whoop) and even magic armor doesn't frequently
polymorph into other magical armor.  Which for my money means that having
wished for SDSM I'd just have to wish for a CoMR or someone's Quest Artifact.
And if I'm not playing a wizard I don't want a CoMR anyway, I want a robe, so
I can spellcast effectively.

Oh!  Plus, while you can't lose SDSM to a polytrap, as far as I know you can
still lose it to a golden naga or other spellcaster with 'destroy armor'.
Maybe golden nagas are friendly to samurai.

So, SDSM: protects from all beam instadeaths, protects equipment from
lightning bolts; doesn't protect from touch of death, needs another wish or
reliance on your stealable Quest artifiact for MR, may force giving up your
robe.

GDSM: protects from touching and wand instadeaths, teleport traps, polytraps,
allows robe, and protects itself from anti-armor attacks.

I stick to the GDSM, except for wizards.

The real question for me is what a Monk should wish for...

